# lf115, the quiet orchard wagerer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf115
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent none
tier standard
written_for cty_sorrel_ashbough
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the quiet orchard wagerer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk cannot_resist_a_wager
likes fried_fish stars festival_bells autumn_wind
dislikes stale_bread bad_manners
fears a_ladder_slipping_under_a_picker a_promise_made_beside_the_stones
hopes an_honest_orchard_wage a_clear_night_after_the_harvest
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.4 memories +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=wry refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# picks #apples#, finds a small #wager# in ordinary work, and watches the old #stones# without claiming knowledge of the past.

words
oath! = By the last apple | Stones and stars
saying! = Count the fruit before the odds | A quiet bet lasts longest
apple = apple | ripe apple
apples = apples | picked apples
fruit = fruit | orchard fruit
orchard = orchard | Plumtree orchard
tree = tree | apple tree
trees = trees | fruit trees
branch = branch | high branch
branches = branches | low branches
ladder = ladder | wooden ladder
rung = rung | ladder rung
basket = basket | woven basket
baskets = baskets | full baskets
crate = crate | fruit crate
crates = crates | stacked crates
store = store | apple store
shelf = shelf | store shelf
bruise = bruise | small bruise
skin = skin | apple skin
stem = stem | short stem
hand = hand | picking hand
hands = hands | working hands
picker = picker | orchard picker
pickers = pickers | orchard pickers
work = work | picking work
wage = wage | day wage
price = price | fruit price
coin = coin | spare coin
market = market | town market
merchant = merchant | fruit merchant
wager = wager | small wager
bet = bet | quiet bet
odds = odds | poor odds
die = die | worn die
dice = dice | old dice
throw = throw | careful throw
win = win | narrow win
loss = loss | small loss
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
newcomer = newcomer | newcomer to town
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
watch = watch | town watch
house = house | shared house
home = home | cottage
door = door | cottage door
window = window | quiet window
road = road | cart road
cart = cart | fruit cart
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
mud = mud | road mud
bread = bread | day-old bread
fish = fish | fried fish
butter = butter | melted butter
meal = meal | late meal
plate = plate | supper plate
larder = larder | thin larder
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | festival bells
festival = festival | town festival
star = star | first star
stars = stars | evening stars
sky = sky | open sky
night = night | clear night
evening = evening | cool evening
autumn = autumn | blustery autumn
wind = wind | autumn wind
rain = rain | cold rain
morning = morning | early morning
day = day | harvest day
stones = stones | standing stones
stone = stone | old stone
mark = mark | worn mark
marks = marks | faded marks
memory = memory | old memory
promise = promise | spoken promise
voice = voice | quiet voice
seat = seat | quiet seat
carts = carts | loaded carts
evenings = evenings | cool evenings
table = table | supper table
plates = plates | empty plates
soil = soil | orchard soil
queue = queue | market queue
city = city | far city

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : A full #plate# would help more than a longer collection. | I count the #coin# passing round.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Too many voices at once. | No one sees the #fruit# until it has a #price#.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I prefer the #bells# from a quiet #window#. | The #queue# at the stall has poor manners.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Their empty benches could hold a #picker# after work. | I have never been asked inside.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : I bring #baskets# out and watch the #price# climb beyond my #wage#. | Someone is winning that #bet#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A fresh #hand# takes a place in the #orchard#. | I want to know who loses the day's #work#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each #autumn# the #fruit# looks much the same. | The #coin# left afterward grows smaller.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The #watch# has questions for every #cart# but no help for a loose #wheel#. | I keep moving.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #baskets# are light this #morning#. | #greet#. I was counting #apples#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I saved a good #apple# for you. | Come in; I have a #wager# worth hearing.
line @1 greet.return : My #ladder# has moved only one #tree# since you left. | You are back before the last #basket# filled.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I saved a #plate# of #fish# for your return. | Take the quiet #seat# near the #window#.
line @1 again.open : I was about to tell you the #odds#. | We had reached the #stone# with the worn #mark#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have another #crate# to carry. | Watch for the #mud# under the #tree#.
line @1 farewell.return : I will count the last #baskets# when you come back. | Another clear #night# will suit me.
line @1 react.news : Who said it first? | I can listen while I sort this #fruit#.
line @1 react.news.new : That has not come up the #road# yet. | Was there a witness?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a different version near the #store#. | Yours has one detail I missed.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would ask whose #hands# were on the #cart#. | That account leaves the #wheel# unexplained.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. You need not speak at once. | I will leave the #fruit# and hear you through.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That is worth the best #apple#. | I may even buy fresh #bread#.
line @1 answer.how : The #fruit# is holding despite the #wind#. | I have had worse #odds# and worked through them.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : This #ladder# needs both my #hands#. | Let me lower the #basket# first.
line @1 ask.how : What did the #road# bring your way today? | Did you see the #stars# last #night#?
line @1 sympathise : Sit with me where it is quiet. | I can find a #meal# after these #crates#.
line @1 reassure : One bad #throw# does not decide a whole #day#. | Daylight may make that #mark# easier to read.
line @1 decline : I will not climb that loose #ladder#. | I cannot make a #promise# on another's behalf.
line @1 accept_decline : Understood. The #basket# stays where it is. | Then let the #bet# rest.
line @1 thank : You steadied the #ladder# when the #wind# rose. | That #fish# was a welcome supper.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I only moved one #crate#. | The #apple# was going to fall anyway.
line @1 preclose : The #store# will close before the #rain#. | I hope the first #star# shows through tonight.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #bet# has more courage than its #odds#. | Even the #ladder# knows when to stop climbing.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #fruit# is sound. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will count it again.
line @1 give.advice : Test the #rung# before reaching for the top #branch#. | Look at the #skin# before setting a #price#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Travel with the other #carts# after dark. | Keep the #coin# out of sight on the #road#.
scene ladder_rung
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I test each #rung# before I climb for the high #fruit#. | A loose one is not worth a full #basket#.
b : Do you find many loose? | Who repairs them?
a : Enough to keep testing. | The #pickers# together.

scene bruised_apple
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A small #bruise# hides under the #skin# until the #apple# is handled. | I put those aside for an early #meal#.
b : Can you sell them? | Do you waste them?
a : For less #coin#. | Never if I can help it.

scene first_basket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first #basket# tells me how the #tree# will yield. | I leave the thin #branches# for later.
b : Why leave them? | How many baskets today?
a : They bend under a load. | That depends on the #wind#.

scene crate_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count #crates# at the #store# after the #cart# unloads. | One missing #crate# is a full #wage# to someone.
b : Have you lost one? | Who signs the count?
a : Not while I watched. | The #store# keeper.

scene stem_twist
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A gentle twist keeps the #stem# with the #apple#. | Pulling hard can tear the #branch#.
b : Does the stem matter? | Is that slower?
a : It tells a buyer something. | Less than fixing the #tree#.

scene orchard_wage
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know the #price# of every #basket# and the #wage# for filling it. | Those numbers do not rise together.
b : Have you asked why? | Who decides?
a : More than once. | The people buying #fruit#.

scene small_wager
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wagered a #coin# on which #tree# would fill a #basket# first. | The slower #picker# won by a single #apple#.
b : Did you pay? | Would you bet again?
a : The #coin# changed hands. | On better #odds#.

scene dice_after_work
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a #die# with worn corners. | It makes every #throw# look suspicious even when it is fair.
b : Do you win often? | Do you cheat?
a : Often enough to play. | I let people wonder.

scene standing_mark
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #mark# on the old #stones# looked different after #rain#. | I think the #stone# kept the memory of whoever cut it.
b : Can stone remember? | Did anyone else see it?
a : I cannot prove it. | One #friend# stood with me.

scene stones_at_dusk
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I pass the #stones# on some #evenings# and leave them untouched. | A spoken #promise# sounds weightier there.
b : Have you made one? | Are you afraid?
a : One, a long time ago. | Only of breaking it.

scene festival_bells
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bells# reach our #window# after the crowd has begun to shout. | I listen from inside until the street is quiet.
b : Do you go out later? | Which bell is first?
a : Sometimes for #fish#. | The small one.

scene fried_fish
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I would spend a little #coin# on #fish# fried in #butter#. | It improves a day of bruised #fruit#.
b : Do you cook it? | Do you share?
a : When I can. | With anyone at the #table#.

scene stale_bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A hard #apple# still beats a stale heel of #bread#. | I soak it rather than throw it away.
b : Does that help? | Why not buy fresh?
a : For supper. | Ask the #merchant#.

scene first_star
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When the #store# closes, I look up through the #branches# for a #star#. | It appears where the upper #branches# make a gap.
b : Can you find it every night? | Do you name it?
a : When the #sky# is clear. | Only for myself.

scene autumn_gust
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A blustery #autumn# strips the weak #apples# before I can pick them. | I gather what the #wind# leaves sound.
b : Does it shorten the work? | Do you like the wind?
a : Not the counting. | From the ground.

scene bad_manners
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A buyer once pushed past the #pickers# to seize the first #basket#. | I made them wait while I checked the #fruit#.
b : Were they angry? | Did they pay?
a : They had time to be. | At the posted #price#.

scene household_cart
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# fills quickly when the other #hands# come home. | I count the empty #plates# before I ask about the #day#.
b : Do they tell you? | Is supper noisy?
a : When they wish. | Less than the #market#.

story loose_ladder [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : The top #rung# gave way as I reached for a #branch#.
  : I dropped the #basket# and caught the #tree# instead.
  b : A wise catch. Were you hurt?
  : Only the #fruit# was bruised.

story wager_on_wind [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I wagered that the #wind# would empty one #tree# by dusk.
  : It spared that #tree# and scattered the next one.
  b : The wind chooses its own side. Did you lose?
  : A single #coin# and a little pride.

story stone_after_rain [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : I noticed a faint #mark# on a #stone# after #rain#.
  : The next dry #day# I could scarcely find it.
  ask : Was it real?
  b : That would stay with me.
  : Real enough for me to leave the #stone# alone.

rule @bark_apple
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Set the bruised #apples# here. | This #basket# is nearly full.

rule @bark_ladder
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Test that #rung# again. | The #ladder# shifts on this #soil#.

rule @bark_bet
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say A small #wager#, then? | I will take the longer #odds#.

rule @bark_stones
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say Leave the old #stones# be. | That #mark# shows after #rain#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have a #basket# to fill. | #greet#. Keep clear of the #ladder#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You remember my last #wager#? | The #store# has another load in.
dlg @1 resident.job : I pick #apples# for #self.workplace#. | I sort #fruit#, fill #crates#, and watch the #ladder#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must count the #baskets#. | #saying.capitalize#. Keep to the #road#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why make a wager? -> wager
node wager
say It gives a long #day# a little shape. I keep the stakes small.
free
choice What do the stones remember? -> stones
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node stones
say I cannot say. I leave their old #marks# as I find them.
choice Back to the orchard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #cart# has just arrived. | #greet#. There may be #fish# tonight.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will cover the #crates#. | Perhaps the #stars# will be clear later.
